NAME
     nice - run a program at another priority

SYNOPSIS
     nice [-n INCREMENT] COMMAND [ARG...]
     renice [-n] VALUE [-p PID | -g PGID | -u USER]...

DESCRIPTION
     nice runs COMMAND with its niceness raised by INCREMENT (10 by
     default): a higher number is a smaller share of the processor.
     Lowering it below zero is root's alone. Called as renice it changes
     a process that is already running.

OPTIONS
     -n N     the increment, or for renice the value
     -p PID   renice: a process
     -g PGID  renice: a process group
     -u USER  renice: a user's processes

SEE ALSO
     taskset(1), cgrun(1), schedbench(1)
